Found live during fahreza's control-primitive testing: tap-text 'Network & internet' failed with 'no UI element matching'. Evidence (android dump) showed the node is text="Network &amp;amp; internet" - uiautomator XML-entity-encodes &,<,>,",'. Root cause: find_node_bounds did tag.contains(format!("text=\"{label}\"")) against RAW xml, and parse_screen_elements returned attr() values raw - so both matching and the screen-map JSON were broken for any label with special chars. Fix: single decode point in attr() (xml_decode; &amp; replaced LAST to avoid double-decode of e.g. &amp;lt;), and find_node_bounds now compares attr()==label (also drops the old raw-substring approach). Note matching stays EXACT-equals (fahreza's 'Network' substring attempt failed separately - by design; forgiving/substring match is a deferred option). Regression test matches_and_decodes_xml_entities added; 7/7 android tests pass. Verified live: tap-text opens the sub-screen, screen-map shows decoded '&', zero '&amp;'.
